(/** @param {any} G */ function (G) {
  "use strict";
  var R = G.LQ_DEPTH = G.LQ_DEPTH || { build: {}, text: { th: {}, en: {}, zh: {} } };
  var T = {"_title":"More from the slip",
    "v.1":"In Thai verse the sun stands for truth and the kindness of elders, while cloud and mist are a stretch when things cannot be seen clearly, not an enemy but a passing veil. Readers take it that what was murky is opening up, and that beyond your small circle there are more roads than you thought.",
    "wish.1":"What you asked for sits at the very favorable level. The sun clearing the cloud says the answer shows itself in pieces, first as small signs such as a word from someone involved or paperwork that starts to move. Keep your eyes open for those signs and build on them at a sensible pace.",
    "work.1":"Look at how you talk with senior people at work. A well-prepared suggestion has a better than usual chance of being heard now, so it is a good time to ask for advice on your long-term path or to volunteer for a part you want to learn, since people can already see what you do.",
    "love.1":"If you are single, an introduction from someone you trust, or a group doing real activities together, is the likelier way to meet a person. If you are with a partner, something hard to say before finds a good moment to be talked through, and both families seem warmer toward each other.",
    "home.1":"The household brightens as if a curtain were drawn back. Elders are in good spirits and ready to advise, so it suits opening windows and rearranging a room, or finally discussing a family plan that was left hanging. If you are thinking of moving, the direction starts to look clearer.",
    "people.1":"Helpers now tend to be older people who have seen your work before, so get back in touch with them. Official or paperwork matters that have been stuck begin to draw someone who points the way. Gather the required documents in full and the matter can move on by itself.",
    "travel.1":"The timing feels like setting out in the morning and finding the sky open. A trip planned long ago tends to become possible once the clouds thin, and on the road you may meet someone with good information or stop at a place new to you. No special day is needed.",
    "lost.1":"A lost item, or something you are waiting for, is like what the cloud has been hiding, and it tends to show once the light reaches it. Retrace that day slowly and ask people who were there. A parcel or a piece of news you await often shows some progress.",
    "v.2":"A seed rooting in damp soil shows growth that happens quietly where no one sees. The rain it waits for is outside timing that must arrive by itself. Readers conclude that buried effort is not wasted, and the leaves that unfurl are a result that appears in season, not when we wish to see it.",
    "wish.2":{"t":"What you asked for is still rooting and has not reached its full harvest. The slip's answer is to keep tending it steadily and let the rain come in its season. Digging up the seed each day to check does not make it grow, so allow a fair stretch of time before judging again.",
    "c":true},
    "work.2":"Look at the skills and working relationships you have built up over a long time that nobody has noticed yet. Keep your results on record, note what you have learned, and be ready to mention it at review time. The payoff tends to arrive as kind words from the people around you.",
    "money.2":"Dropping coins in a jar regularly works better than waiting for one big sum. Money you lent may come back in small installments within what the borrower can manage. In trade, modest profit with steady sales suits you more than waiting for one sale that pays everything back.",
    "love.2":"A newly started relationship needs time, like a seedling. If you are single and talking with someone, there is no need to rush to name it. If you are together, trust stored up from small everyday things is helping both families accept each other more.",
    "home.2":"The household is the damp soil that holds warmth. Tending plants, cooking together or visiting elders regularly will slowly deepen closeness. Small repairs you have put off for a long time suit being done one spot at a time.",
    "people.2":"Old friends, or people you once helped, begin to message you again. Checking in now and then is the watering that keeps small ties alive. For paperwork, submit everything complete, keep copies, and wait through the steps calmly.",
    "travel.2":"Short trips close to home suit this slip, such as visiting relatives, going to a garden or walking by the water. For a bigger trip farther away, save and plan ahead like a seed waiting for its season, then move forward one step at a time.",
    "lost.2":"Lost things tend to be near where you last put them. Search thoroughly in the usual corners before looking far away. What you are waiting for is like a seed awaiting rain, and when the moment comes it can show itself.",
    "v.3":"The boat in the verse stands for a life under way. A tailwind is support from circumstances that you did not have to build yourself, and the northern shore is the destination the boat is heading for. Readers take it as a time to raise the sail, and still hold the rudder true.",
    "wish.3":"What you asked for sits at the very favorable level. Outside timing is on your side, so the answer may come sooner than you counted on. Just set your own bearings and say plainly what you want, because a good wind helps most the boat that knows where it is going.",
    "work.3":{"t":"Work moves fast enough that small details are easy to skip. Before you send something off or close a deal, check the figures and the terms once more and keep your team informed in time. Speed helps as long as the boat is still in the channel.",
    "c":true},
    "love.3":"If you are single, you may get to know someone through a trip or a shared activity. If you are with a partner, it suits talking about plans you could carry out together, such as a long trip or saving toward a shared goal, sincerely and at a natural pace.",
    "people.3":"Helpers come quickly. An old friend from a different line of work may introduce you to someone new. Official paperwork is likely to be done on time or sooner than expected, as long as you have copies and supporting papers ready in advance.",
    "travel.3":"A tailwind suits a longer journey. The way out tends to be easy, with good things met on the road. Leave some spare time on the way back so you can enjoy the route fully. Trips connected with work or learning also go well.",
    "lost.3":"Things you are waiting for, such as a parcel, a document or news, tend to arrive quickly on the wind. For a lost item, retrace the route you took that day briskly but without flurry, and you will often find it along the same path.",
    "v.4":"In Thai belief the lotus bud is a mind still developing, and something that must wait for its moment. Morning light is the opportunity that arrives in its own time, not ours. Not prying the petals open is the heart of the verse: prepare, and trust the timing on its way.",
    "wish.4":{"t":"What you asked for is not yet ready to open. Do not push for a quick answer or press people for one. Use this time to get yourself and your heart ready, and when the morning light arrives, the petals will unfold more beautifully than if you had pried them.",
    "c":true},
    "work.4":{"t":"It is not yet the time to put yourself forward or push for a new position. Use this stretch to update your skills, organize your portfolio and build trust with those around you. The right opportunity arrives once you are ready for it, with no need to run ahead of time.",
    "c":true},
    "love.4":{"t":"Do not rush to ask for answers or push for a label on the relationship. Give the feelings on both sides time to grow. If you are single, there is no need to worry about not having anyone. If you are together, spend time on simple things with no agenda.",
    "c":true},
    "home.4":"The home has a calm mood like the morning before the light comes. Elders in the household like a slow, steady rhythm, such as breakfast together or quiet prayer or reflection in each person's own way. Small shared routines help everyone feel at ease.",
    "people.4":"The right helper appears in its own time, often someone you have known for a long while who gets a chance to assist. Keep up your relationships steadily. For paperwork, file according to the steps and follow up politely.",
    "travel.4":{"t":"There is no need to hurry off. Choose a day that suits you and leave once your preparations are done. Rushed trips tend to miss what is worth seeing, and if things are not yet settled, you can put it off without worry.",
    "c":true},
    "lost.4":{"t":"For a lost item or news you await, do not tear the place apart in a hurry. Rest your mind for a moment, then recall things one spot at a time. Things often show up when you are calm. What you are waiting for still needs a little more time.",
    "c":true},
    "v.5":"In Thai verse a traveling companion is a kalyanamitta, a good friend who walks beside you and does not leave. The two mountains are a task that looks big but can be crossed with a friend to steady you. Readers see your strength in your bonds with people, not in effort alone.",
    "wish.5":"What you asked for moves forward through the goodwill of others, perhaps a suggestion from a friend or acquaintance who opens a door. You do not have to carry everything alone. Tell the people close to you what you are looking for, because help often comes from where you did not expect it.",
    "work.5":"A team with one shared goal makes heavy work lighter. Try dividing tasks by each person's strengths, and invite coworkers to give you their honest opinion. A view from someone else can reveal a shortcut that you overlooked.",
    "money.5":{"t":"Someone points you to a source of income. Listen, then check it out yourself carefully before deciding, ask for details and give yourself time to think. If you go into business with a friend, agree on roles and shares in writing.",
    "c":true},
    "love.5":"Love gets support from the people around you. A friend may introduce someone who suits you, or help a person in a relationship see the other side more clearly. Bringing your partner into your circle of friends is a sincere gesture that works well.",
    "home.5":"The family helps one another as if walking together. Try dividing chores and responsibilities clearly. Elders at home are glad to listen, and for a big household decision such as a renovation, sitting down together as a whole family settles it better.",
    "people.5":"Helpers come from several directions now, among them classmates, neighbors and people in the same line of work. For paperwork or dealing with offices, having someone come along or check that everything is complete greatly reduces confusion.",
    "travel.5":"Traveling in a group or with a close friend is fun and reassuring. Help each other with maps, driving and carrying bags. The two mountains in the verse may hint at a route over hills or high ground, so prepare sensibly for that.",
    "lost.5":"A lost item has often been seen or kept by someone. Ask your travel companions, family or coworkers, and try posting in a relevant group. What you are waiting for will have people helping to follow it up.",
    "v.6":"The full moon in Thai verse is a picture of fullness and cool kindness. A clear sky means a mind that is not clouded, and soft light is brightness that does not sting the eyes. Readers take it as a time when good intentions are noticed and answered gently.",
    "wish.6":"What you asked for sits at the very favorable level. Like a full moon everyone looks up and sees together, the answer tends to come clearly with people glad for you. Thank those who quietly helped you earlier, and the fulfillment will feel warmer still.",
    "work.6":"Your work has a chance of being mentioned in a meeting or in front of seniors. Prepare a short summary and remember to name the colleagues who worked on it with you. That keeps your reputation in a gentle, lasting light.",
    "money.6":"Money falls into a fitting place. It may not be a big sum, but income and spending are in balance, which suits paying off a small outstanding debt or saving for a gift for someone you love. Giving in measure keeps your heart light and your hands from running empty.",
    "love.6":"Love is a time of warm contentment. If you are single, you may meet someone with whom things feel calm and natural. If you are together, quiet evenings of listening to each other suit you. Both families tend to be open and glad.",
    "home.6":"The home feels warm, as if softly lit. Family members get along, which suits gathering relatives, sharing a meal or showing respect to elders with small acts of care. Old lingering matters ease more readily.",
    "people.6":"People around you are ready to be kind, and friends or elders who drifted apart may start talking again. With paperwork or offices, officials or advisers tend to explain things patiently. Ask until it is clear and write it down.",
    "travel.6":"Evening and night travel have an especially good mood now. It suits a train ride, a boat trip or a walk by the water as the moon rises. Choose places with good lighting and a fair number of people so you can fully relax.",
    "lost.6":"A lost item has a chance of being found once your mind is calm. Sit and recall things in a relaxed way before you start searching. The soft moonlight says the answer will not be hard to find. What you are waiting for tends to arrive when your heart is ready for it.",
    "v.7":"The small stream in Thai verse stands for a gentleness that does not give up. The rock is an obstacle that needs no smashing, because water can go around it, and the sea is a destination larger than oneself. Readers take it that the route may bend, but if you do not stop, you can arrive.",
    "wish.7":{"t":"What you asked for will get there, but perhaps not by the straight road you pictured. You have to accept some detours and change your method when you meet a stone. Do not hold to one plan tightly, and keep a second option ready so you are not frustrated when the first is blocked.",
    "c":true},
    "work.7":{"t":"If the usual way is stuck, change your method before you change your goal, for example by asking a different person for input, changing when you present, or breaking the task into smaller pieces. Do not push straight against it, because the roundabout way may be faster.",
    "c":true},
    "money.7":{"t":"Make your financial plan more flexible and leave room in the budget for unplanned costs. Do not tie all your money to a single path. If income slows, trim unnecessary spending first, then look for new channels calmly.",
    "c":true},
    "love.7":"Being big-hearted and willing to forgive lets love flow. If you are single, do not cling too tightly to a dream picture of a person. If you are together, hear the other person's reasons before you answer. Small quarrels are like rocks, and gentle words go around them.",
    "home.7":"There may be small differences at home over space or house rules. Use the flexibility of water and take turns adjusting, and elders at home will see your good will. Setting aside time and a corner for each person eases the tightness.",
    "people.7":"When you meet someone who thinks differently from you, see them as another stream. Listen first, then answer. Paperwork sent back for correction is no big mistake, just a step. Fix it fully and resubmit as you were advised.",
    "travel.7":{"t":"The way there may involve a detour or a change of route, so leave spare time and have a backup plan. If a ticket or a booking has to move, do not be frustrated at once, since the changed route may lead to something you did not expect.",
    "c":true},
    "lost.7":{"t":"A lost item may have moved from where you thought. Search from a corner you would not normally think of, and do not rush to conclude it is gone. What you are waiting for may come slowly and by a roundabout way, yet it tends to arrive if you keep following it.",
    "c":true},
    "v.8":"In Thai belief a lamp stands for wisdom and goodness that can be passed on. The first flame does not dim when it lights others, so the image says that what is given grows. Readers take it that generosity and teaching are the road that brightens your own life and the lives around you.",
    "wish.8":"What you asked for moves forward through sharing. Try helping someone who is looking for something like what you want. The knowledge, information or time you give tends to circle back in a form you did not expect, and once you have received, remember to light someone else's lamp too.",
    "work.8":"Try volunteering to coach a junior colleague or writing a short guide for the team. Passing on knowledge makes you someone the unit can lean on. Seniors notice leadership, and openings on new projects tend to go first to people with a generous spirit.",
    "money.8":{"t":"Give and share within your means, but always set aside your regular expenses and a reserve first. Do not lend more than you could bear to lose if it is not repaid. Giving that does not squeeze yourself is the light that lasts.",
    "c":true},
    "love.8":"Love grows from attention to the other person's details, such as remembering what they like or helping with what worries them. If you are single, you may meet someone through volunteering or a group that helps others. If you are together, try doing a good deed side by side.",
    "home.8":"At home and nearby, sharing food, supplies or time with neighbors warms the whole lane. Elders feel glad to see the young being kind. It suits making merit or doing small activities together as a family.",
    "people.8":"Your network widens through kindness, and people you once helped will think of you. With paperwork, try helping a friend fill in a form or go along with them. You will learn the steps better and have company when you file your own.",
    "travel.8":"Trips connected with volunteering, visiting the elderly, or helping at a community event bring a full heart. On the way you may meet people with the same intentions and come home with a new outlook.",
    "lost.8":"A lost item may turn up after you ask others to help, so tell people close by and those in the relevant place. On the other side, helping someone else look for their thing is light that returns. Something you are waiting for often sees good things happen while you wait.",
    "v.9":"The golden dragon in Thai and Chinese symbolism stands for honor, the power of elders and what has been stored up for years until the day of flight. The blue sky is wide space with no ceiling. Readers take it that the fruit of long effort becomes visible to others and is built by your own hands.",
    "wish.9":"What you asked for sits at the very favorable level. Success arrives as a result you built yourself, not drifting luck, and the soaring dragon says what you intended can come true in plain view. Look back over what you have already done and thank yourself once.",
    "work.9":"There is a chance of a promotion or a big assignment. Have your portfolio, figures and examples ready before it is discussed. Advice from a senior you respect helps you step into the new role smoothly, especially where you will be looking after more people.",
    "money.9":"Income tends to rise from your results, and pay or a bonus may be better than before. It is a good time to negotiate fair compensation, both in a regular job and in contract work. Set aside some to thank the people who helped push you forward.",
    "love.9":"Love is steady and you are proud of each other, and families tend to accept you when they see your results. If you are single, you will draw people who admire your ability, so look at respect and sincerity more than at the surface.",
    "home.9":"The elders at home are proud of you. There may be a chance for a small celebration of someone's success in the family. It suits making the home look dignified and orderly to receive the new opportunities coming in.",
    "people.9":{"t":"When your name rises, more eyes turn your way. Stay humble and read every contract carefully before you sign. If someone offers to come close, give it a little time to get to know them before trusting them with anything important.",
    "c":true},
    "travel.9":"Work travel, such as a meeting, a site visit or accepting an award, tends to give more than you expect. Carry your documents and business cards, since someone may be interested in working with you along the way.",
    "lost.9":"Things you await, such as a job application result, a decision or a reply, have a good chance of coming back favorably. A lost item is usually not far from where you work or use it often, so go through your bag, folders or desk again carefully.",
    "v.10":"Bamboo in Thai verse is a plant that is strong yet bends. Planted once, it spreads by itself and gives shade, poles and shoots. Planting it beside the house is an investment of time. Readers take it that what you set down today will be something your household can lean on for years.",
    "wish.10":"What you asked for is something that slowly forms the base of your life, not something that ends in one day. What you start laying down with care now will give shade later. Write down one long-term goal and finish its first step.",
    "work.10":"This suits setting up work systems, writing out procedures or making long-term agreements clear. The reliability you build now becomes your name in the field. If you are thinking of changing jobs, pick a place where you can learn and stand on a firm footing.",
    "love.10":"This is plain love without fireworks that you can trust. If you are single, you may be drawn to someone warm and dependable. If you are together, try planning small futures such as arranging the home or saving toward a shared goal, and both families can come to accept it more easily.",
    "people.10":"Neighbors and old friends are people to rely on, and relationships you have tended for years repay you. With paperwork, keeping your files orderly in one place makes dealing with offices easier for a long time to come.",
    "travel.10":"Going home or revisiting a familiar place brings warmth. A well-known route lowers worry, and it suits bringing family along and spending unhurried time on ordinary things such as shade trees and familiar meals.",
    "lost.10":"A lost item is usually at home or close by. Check behind the cabinets, under the bed and in old bags. What you are waiting for may come slowly, but it comes solid and useful for a long time, such as an important document you can use for years.",
    "v.11":{"t":"Morning mist hiding a mountain peak stands for a matter that is unclear because information is incomplete, not because it is dangerous. The words a little later say clarity depends on time and the sun reaching it. Readers take it to walk carefully and not decide while the path is hidden.","c":true},
    "wish.11":{"t":"What you asked for is not clear enough to decide on. Wait for the information to come in and for the mist to thin. Do not hurry to accept or refuse. Write down the questions still open and answer them one by one, and the whole picture will sharpen as the morning goes on.",
    "c":true},
    "work.11":{"t":"It is not yet wise to decide something big, such as changing jobs or taking a new project, until you know all the conditions. Ask for more information, talk to someone who has been through something similar, and give yourself a night or two before answering.",
    "c":true},
    "money.11":{"t":"Do not rush to put in a large sum or sign a financial contract you have not fully read. Check the fees and conditions, take time to compare several places, and if you are unsure, ask a knowledgeable person who has nothing to gain.",
    "c":true},
    "love.11":{"t":"If something is weighing on you, ask directly in a gentle voice rather than guessing. If you are single, do not read too much into anyone's manner, and let it become clear before you attach your heart. If you are together, listen to the end before you conclude.",
    "c":true},
    "home.11":"For household matters that are still unclear, such as plans to renovate or to care for an elder, a calm chat in good weather helps. Elders can make the picture clear. Jot down a short agreement so everyone understands the same thing.",
    "people.11":{"t":"With paperwork or dealing with offices, do not sign or confirm what you do not yet understand. Ask for it to be explained again until it is clear and keep a copy. With people, spend time getting to know them before giving trust.",
    "c":true},
    "travel.11":{"t":"Check the route, the weather and the timing well before you set off. If mist comes down or information is missing, you can postpone a little. Leaving a bit later and seeing the road clearly will give you more peace of mind.",
    "c":true},
    "lost.11":{"t":"A lost item may not turn up just yet. Set it aside for a short while and come back with fresher eyes. For what you are waiting for, news or an answer may not have come, so do not read meaning into the silence.",
    "c":true},
    "v.12":"A bird carrying straw one piece at a time to build a nest is a picture of building a home with perseverance. Each strand is worth little, but together they make a shelter for the young. Readers take it that lasting warmth comes from small things gathered every day, not from one big effort.",
    "wish.12":"What you asked for succeeds by gathering small bits together. Break the goal into small tasks that can be done in a day and do them regularly. Visible progress is encouraging and draws what you asked for closer.",
    "work.12":"Work does better through systems and routine than through bursts of enthusiasm. Set a daily time for the important task, make a checklist and keep a progress log. Piled up over time, it becomes results anyone can see.",
    "love.12":"Love grows from small, steady attention, such as a message to ask how they are, a small gift or a meal together. If you are single and have met no one, make the place you live warm and true to yourself, since a warm heart draws people on its own.",
    "home.12":"The home warms up one corner at a time. It suits arranging the house room by room and adding needed items one by one. If you are preparing to move into a new place or welcome a newcomer such as a baby or a pet, prepare things ahead step by step.",
    "people.12":"Friends who complete one another are like a nesting pair. Small relationships tended regularly are steadier than a large circle. For paperwork, filing each paper in order by date saves a great deal of time later.",
    "travel.12":"Short trips near home that you do regularly, such as a weekend market, a bike ride or a day at a relative's house, bring simple happiness. If you want to go far, save and gather information a little at a time beforehand.",
    "lost.12":"Small items such as a button, an earring or a key are usually in a place you use regularly. Check the spots of your routine one by one. What you are waiting for will come in parts rather than all at once.",
    "v.13":"A full ear of rice bows down, an image Thai people use to teach humility in capable people. The later line says the field is not too hot and the rain comes in season, a fitting balance. Readers take it as harvest time, and humility keeps the harvest with you longer.",
    "wish.13":"What you asked for sits at the very favorable level. Like rice in harvest season, what you planted will give the result you intended. When you receive it, share a part and thank everyone who helped, since fullness that is not hoarded lasts longer.",
    "work.13":"Your results are plain to see and you may be recognized. Share credit with your team and thank your supporters in front of others, which adds to the respect you receive. It is a good time to sum up lessons and teach those who follow.",
    "money.13":"Finances are abundant and income arrives by season or by cycle. It suits storing a portion in the granary, as farmers keep seed for next year, and setting some aside for merit or caring for parents. Wealth that can be shared lasts.",
    "love.13":"Love is warm like family. If you are single, you may meet someone kind who values family as you do. If you are together, it suits planning life together and introducing each other to relatives, and a humble manner softens the elders.",
    "home.13":"The home is rich in warmth and the elders are in a generous mood. It suits cooking a big meal together, harvesting from the kitchen garden or going back to look after the old family home. Recipes and stories from elders are treasures worth writing down.",
    "people.13":"People who once helped you will come back, see the result and be glad. Write or call to thank them in a special way. With paperwork, the people concerned tend to cooperate now, and a polite manner makes the steps go through easily.",
    "travel.13":"Visiting elderly relatives or going back to your home province brings full happiness. Bring gifts out of goodwill. A route past fields and gardens can open up your mind, and it suits real rest.",
    "lost.13":"A lost item may come back thanks to your humble manner, for example by asking politely and thanking those who kept it safe. What you are waiting for, such as money owed or a result, tends to arrive in its full season.",
    "v.14":"The wooden bridge in the verse links two banks divided by a canal. Hearts meeting halfway means no one has to cross all the way over. Readers see that conflict or distance eases by walking half the way and listening the other half.",
    "wish.14":"What you asked for can succeed through compromise. Consider what you could let go of in order to get what you need, and ask the other side what they want. The answer tends to lie in the middle, where both sides can live.",
    "work.14":"This suits negotiation or coordinating between departments, and you may be asked to act as go-between. Prepare the points you can bend on separately from those you cannot. Hear out what the other side needs before you propose, and the agreement will fit well.",
    "love.14":"Patching up understanding in love goes well, and people who drifted apart have a chance to talk again. Be the one who walks halfway with sincerity. For differences between two families, look for common ground that everyone is comfortable with.",
    "home.14":"Relatives on two sides, or members who see things differently, have a chance to understand each other more. An elder may act as the bridge. On dividing property or sharing the care of parents, sit down with everyone present and respect each view.",
    "people.14":"You or someone close may be the link that helps two groups meet. With contracts, check that they are fair to both sides and have a witness or a copy. A trustworthy go-between helps matters end neatly.",
    "travel.14":"This suits traveling to meet an important person or to negotiate something that needs to be discussed in person. Meeting face to face tends to work better than messages. Fix the time and place clearly and arrive a little early.",
    "lost.14":"A lost item may be with someone you met along the way, such as a restaurant, a vehicle or a friend's workplace. Contact those places politely. What you are waiting for resolves when you communicate directly.",
    "v.15":"A small boat waiting for the tide to fill is a picture of not forcing nature. Tides rise and fall on their own schedule, and shoving a boat across dry mud spends effort without going anywhere. Readers take it as time to prepare: check the ropes, load supplies, set out when the water is ready.",
    "wish.15":{"t":"What you asked for still has to wait for the tide. Pushing now would be wasted effort. Use the wait to prepare what is missing, such as information, papers or helpers. When the moment comes you can launch at once and with far less strain.",
    "c":true},
    "work.15":{"t":"Do not rush to close a piece of work or push a proposal whose time has not come. Use this period to tighten the plan, rehearse your presentation and talk with the people involved so everyone understands the same thing. When the window opens, the work moves without needing to be redone.",
    "c":true},
    "love.15":{"t":"Do not press the other person to decide or hurry the relationship along. Give each other time. Use this stretch to know yourself, what you want and where your limits are. When the water is full, clarity comes by itself.",
    "c":true},
    "home.15":{"t":"A move or a major renovation should wait until the costs and the timing are more ready. Elders at home may need time to think, so do not pressure them. Use this period to gather information and set money aside.",
    "c":true},
    "people.15":"Helpers and the right people are getting ready as well. If a meeting is not yet fixed, do not worry. With paperwork, check that everything to be attached is complete and file in the round when the office is open to receive it, so you do not make a wasted trip.",
    "travel.15":{"t":"It is fine to postpone a trip if it is not convenient. Check dates, travel conditions and what you need to prepare, then choose a day when everything is ready. Waiting does not cost you the opportunity.",
    "c":true},
    "lost.15":{"t":"For a lost item, do not tear everywhere apart in haste. Pause a while and think back to when you used it last. What you are waiting for still needs time, and asking too often does not make it arrive sooner.",
    "c":true},
    "v.16":"The North Star in the verse is the point that does not move, used as a fixed mark for direction since sailing days. When the sky is dark and no shore is in sight, readers take it that a mind anchored in its own values does not lose its way, even when no one is pointing.",
    "wish.16":"What you asked for sits at the very favorable level. Ask yourself whether it really agrees with what you believe and value. If it does, the path will clear by itself. If not, this slip invites a small adjustment of the request so that it matches your own principles.",
    "work.16":"When you must decide something at work, use your own principles as the compass, such as honesty toward clients, quality of the work or fairness to the team, and the choices narrow down to the right one. Seniors see this steadiness and trust you.",
    "money.16":"Set your financial goals clearly, such as how much to save in how many months, and write them where you see them daily. Accurate planning keeps you from chasing spending trends. Try keeping a separate account for a big goal.",
    "love.16":"Love begins with knowing what you want in a partnership. If you are single and clear about your principles, it is easier to filter for someone compatible. If you are together, talk about shared values such as family, money and home.",
    "home.16":"The home has clear principles, and elders are the pillar who points the direction. Decisions about the house are easier when everyone sees the same goal. Try writing a short set of house rules or a long-range plan together and posting it where all can see.",
    "people.16":"An adviser or teacher who points the way may appear. Choose to listen to people who behave well and have real experience. With paperwork, follow the stated steps without skipping any, and it goes through without having to come back to fix it.",
    "travel.16":{"t":"A long journey goes smoothly when route and destination are planned clearly. The North Star reminds you to carry a map or navigation app and to tell someone close where you are going. It suits trips with a clear purpose, such as study or a meeting.","c":true},
    "lost.16":"A lost item can be found by using a system: retrace events in order and check key places one at a time. There is no need to panic. What you are waiting for will arrive from the direction you set, if you follow up in an orderly way.",
    "v.17":"The first rain of the season in Thai verse is a picture of relief and fresh starts. Cracked ground is not barren, it is only waiting for water, and once it gets it, it turns green fast. Readers take it that a dry period, in both energy and spirit, is passing.",
    "wish.17":"What you asked for is reviving like a field after the first rain. Signs of change may be a small piece of news or an encouraging word. Accept them, and answer with a small action you had put on hold.",
    "work.17":{"t":"Work comes back to life, but there is no need to gather everything at once and run yourself dry again. Take the backlog one matter at a time and schedule rest for yourself as well. Greet the team you drifted from, which is a good moment to begin again together.",
    "c":true},
    "money.17":"Finances start to ease bit by bit. It suits settling small debts that were left, picking up the side work that went quiet, and starting to save again with an amount you are comfortable with. Money turns back with the season, like water refilling the land.",
    "love.17":"The heart comes back refreshed after a weary stretch. If you are single, you can begin to open to someone new again. If you are together, understanding that faded returns through gentle talk, and small apologies carry great power now.",
    "home.17":"The mood at home lightens like dust washed off by rain. It suits a big clean, rearranging a room, changing curtains or planting something new. Elders who have been worried relax when they see the family coming back to life.",
    "people.17":"People you drifted from begin to get in touch, so answer with an open mind. Paperwork or contacts that have been pending a long time start to show progress. Follow up politely and have your information ready.",
    "travel.17":"A trip for a change of scenery helps restore your spirits. Mountains, sea or green countryside suit this slip. It does not need to be far or costly, only a while away from the usual place.",
    "lost.17":"A lost item tends to appear when you wash or reorganize a space, such as during a house clean. For what you are waiting for, good news about a contact or a refund starts to show signs.",
    "v.18":"A climber resting in the shade of a tree is an image Thai people use to teach that rest is not defeat. A high peak calls for breathing in stages. Readers take the big goal as the mountain, and those who know how to rest reach the top more surely than those who rush until they are spent.",
    "wish.18":{"t":"What you asked for is a large goal, and it should not be expected to arrive in one go. Divide it into stages, rest when tired, then walk on. This slip does not say you will not succeed, only that you need to ration your strength to reach the end.",
    "c":true},
    "work.18":{"t":"Divide the big job into clear stages, each with a goal and a rest day. Do not let work pile up until it overwhelms you. Tell your manager plainly if the load is too heavy so deadlines can be adjusted to something reasonable.",
    "c":true},
    "money.18":{"t":"Set money goals in steps, such as building the first month's reserve and then moving to the next target. Do not save so hard that you have too little to live on day to day, and do not make big decisions while tired or anxious.",
    "c":true},
    "love.18":"Spend restful time together, such as watching the sunset or eating slowly. Love does not have to hurry to the next stage. If you are single, there is no need to rush to find someone because of age or what others say. If you are together, give each other a short span of attention every day.",
    "home.18":"At home, let everyone have their own time to rest. Elders need a pace that is not pushed. Try arranging a seat in the shade or by a window as a place to rest the mind, and share out unfinished chores a little at a time.",
    "people.18":"A friend you can trust is one who lets you rest and does not nag. For paperwork, do it in stages, such as collecting proofs today, filling the form tomorrow and filing the day after, so it is not too heavy and nothing is missed.",
    "travel.18":{"t":"Travel unhurried, stop to rest at intervals and leave time for rest along the way. If the route is long, break it into legs and do not push on when tired. The destination can wait.",
    "c":true},
    "lost.18":{"t":"If you cannot find something, stop and rest before searching on. A tired mind often overlooks what is in front of it. What you are waiting for is still on the road, so do not run after it, and wait with an easy mind.",
    "c":true},
    "v.19":"The clear mirror in Thai verse is a picture of seeing yourself as you are, not to judge but to adjust until it fits. The second line says that a small adjustment brings affection. Readers take it that small changes born of self-understanding carry more power than a big overhaul.",
    "wish.19":"What you asked for settles when you adjust small things in yourself, such as how you speak, how you use your time or how you treat the people involved. Ask one trusted person what they see that could be adjusted, then pick the item you can do right away.",
    "work.19":"Changing how you communicate, such as summing up in clear points, listening before answering or replying to messages on time, will make work flow much better. Ask a trusted coworker for feedback and try one suggestion this week.",
    "money.19":{"t":"Try reviewing the last month of spending and you will find unneeded items you can trim, such as subscriptions you do not use or things bought twice. Adjust there and more money is left without cutting what matters.",
    "c":true},
    "love.19":"Love grows sweeter with small adjustments, such as listening more, saying thank you more often, or setting aside time together without phones. If you are single, look at your own image and daily habits, and be a version of yourself that is comfortable and well cared for.",
    "home.19":"At home, let everyone hold up the mirror and see which rules or routines no longer fit. Adjust them together in a warm mood. Elders like to see the young listening. Keeping the home airy and clean lightens the mind.",
    "people.19":"People around you reflect how you treat them, so start with a sincere greeting. For paperwork, check that names, spellings and numbers match on every document before filing so the matter goes through smoothly.",
    "travel.19":"Before a trip, check that you have everything, such as documents, daily necessities and chargers, and write a list to tick off. Good preparation makes a trip easy and saves you from fixing problems at the destination.",
    "lost.19":"A lost item is often somewhere you have already looked at but not noticed. Walk through again slowly, studying as closely as you would a mirror. For what you are waiting for, check that your contact details are right, as a message may have slipped through.",
    "v.20":"The big bodhi tree in Thai culture stands for shade, calm and wisdom. People often rest under a large tree with trust, and elders who are fond of you are like that shade. Readers take it that a patron or teacher offers support without being asked.",
    "wish.20":"What you asked for sits at the very favorable level. An elder or an experienced person can ease the way. State what you need politely and directly, since such people are often glad to point the way or speak for you. When it works out, remember to go back and thank them.",
    "work.20":"A boss or senior colleague may push you toward an opportunity, such as recommending you for a project or speaking for you in a meeting. Show your readiness and ask advice on your career path. Elders are ready to teach and open doors for those who are earnest.",
    "money.20":"An elder who knows about money may help you see options, such as planning savings or handling debt. Listen from several angles and choose what fits you. Pay and benefits from the organization that looks after you may improve.",
    "love.20":"Your family supports your love. A fond elder may help introduce someone or open their heart to the person you choose. If you are single, you may meet someone at a merit-making event, a wedding or a community activity where an elder gives it trust.",
    "home.20":"The home is warm and safe, as if a great shade tree covered it. Elders are kind and glad to give advice, which suits consulting them on moving or renovating, and spending time hearing their stories to receive an inheritance of the heart.",
    "people.20":"A kind patron, teacher or adviser may appear. Show respect and thanks. With paperwork or dealing with offices, someone experienced helps point out where to go and whom to contact, which cuts confusion a great deal.",
    "travel.20":"Wherever you go there tends to be someone to help, such as a friendly fellow passenger, a local who points the way or a relative who welcomes you. It suits a trip to meet an elder you respect or to learn from someone knowledgeable.",
    "lost.20":"A lost item often has a kind person who has kept it or will get in touch. Ask elders at the place, such as a shop owner or the staff in charge. For what you are waiting for, an elder helps speed it along or takes care of it for you.",
    "v.21":"Worker bees in Thai symbolism stand for diligence with order. Each has its duty and flies back to the hive every day. Honey is sweet because it is gathered from thousands of flowers. Readers take it that success is the product of discipline and working together, not of a single special talent.",
    "wish.21":"What you asked for succeeds through steady diligence. What you do every day is storing nectar. Write one thing you can do today and finish it. What you see in the comb will tell you that you are on the right track.",
    "work.21":"Your diligence is starting to be seen. Build a clear work routine with a place to record results. A team that works together systematically does well, and you may be given a role that involves coordinating more of the team.",
    "money.21":"Income comes from earnest work, performance-based pay or side income from your skill. Try setting part aside as a common pot, like the hive, for times of need or chances to grow.",
    "love.21":"Love is building a future together through small daily work, such as sharing chores or planning finances together. If you are single, you may meet someone diligent with similar goals through work or an activity done together.",
    "home.21":"The home is a hive that everyone helps look after. Try making a clear chore chart. Elders appreciate seeing cooperation. A small vegetable plot, or cooking food that keeps for several days, suits this period.",
    "people.21":"Diligent teammates and coworkers will be the group that helps you. For paperwork, make it a routine, for example clearing the backlog once a week so it does not pile up and force a rush at the last minute.",
    "travel.21":"Travel to learn, such as training, a study visit or visiting a business that does what interests you, brings full benefit. Take notes and exchange contacts, which become a stock you can use for a long time.",
    "lost.21":"A lost item tends to turn up when you search systematically. Divide the area into sections and search one at a time without repeating. What you are waiting for, such as payment or an approval document, usually comes once you have done your own part in full.",
    "v.22":"Bamboo that bends in a strong wind and springs back upright is an image Thai people use to teach strong gentleness. A stiff tree often snaps in a storm, while bamboo yields and survives. Readers take it that bowing when the wind is fiercest is not surrender but a way of keeping the roots.",
    "wish.22":{"t":"What you asked for can succeed through flexibility rather than insisting on one way. If some conditions change, adjust your manner to the situation and keep what matters most. Do not force it when the wind is strong, and stand upright again once it eases.",
    "c":true},
    "work.22":{"t":"Hear differing opinions calmly, and do not answer at once when someone criticizes you. Separate the work from your sense of self, note what you can use to adjust, and reply once your feelings settle. Stepping back one pace may bring cooperation back three.",
    "c":true},
    "money.22":{"t":"Keep a reserve that covers several months, which is the bamboo's shade. Do not tie all your money to a single plan, and do not take on installments that are too tight. If income fluctuates, trim the expenses you can adjust first.",
    "c":true},
    "love.22":"Gentleness is the key to love. Try swapping argument for listening first. If you are single, do not be so rigid about criteria that you overlook a good person. If you are together, soft words and giving way sometimes build trust that can stand the wind.",
    "home.22":"Elders at home may see things differently from the younger generation. Listen with respect, then meet in the middle without trying to win. On routines or use of space, take turns being flexible, and the whole household becomes warmer.",
    "people.22":"When you meet someone stiff or willful, bend in the way you speak while keeping your own principles. With paperwork, if you are asked to correct it or add information, do so politely, which is faster than arguing over procedure.",
    "travel.22":{"t":"Keep a backup in your travel plans, such as a flight or bus at two times or a booking that can be cancelled. If the weather or situation changes, postpone or reroute without irritation.",
    "c":true},
    "lost.22":{"t":"For a lost item, do not search in a tense way. Loosen up, soften your mind and look with a light hand. The item has often not gone far. What you are waiting for may arrive slightly changed in form, so be open to the new shape.","c":true},
    "v.23":"A rainbow in Thai verse appears when light passes through raindrops, an image of beauty that can come out of a hard stretch. The drizzle stands for the tiring time, and the colors signal that the sky has opened. Readers take it that what you hoped for is coming into view, with colors to cheer you.",
    "wish.23":"What you asked for sits at the very favorable level. After a long wait and patience, the hope is coming true like a rainbow when the rain eases. Pause and look back at how well you got through, then open your heart to the good that follows.",
    "work.23":"Good news about work arrives like the sky opening, such as an evaluation result, a new position or a client returning. Send a thank-you to the people who encouraged you through the hard time, so that your relationships at work stay bright for a long while.",
    "money.23":{"t":"Finances improve noticeably, but wait for the money to actually arrive before planning how to spend it. Do not spend ahead on confidence. Keep part aside as protection for when rain comes again, and you will feel at ease for a long time.",
    "c":true},
    "love.23":"Love is bright like a fresh start. Someone who has just come through something sad may begin to open their heart. For a couple who had clouds between them, this is a fine moment to begin again together, such as going somewhere new or doing something you have never done.",
    "home.23":"The home has a bright mood after a tense period. Elders smile more easily. It suits holding a meal or taking a family photo as a keepsake. The happiness that follows at home is a small color worth saving.",
    "people.23":"Misunderstandings between people begin to clear, and good news from friends or helpers is likely to come in. Paperwork that went through a long process starts to show a satisfying result. Thank everyone involved at each step.",
    "travel.23":"Traveling after rain, or after a heavy stretch of work, gives you lovely views and joy, such as scenery after a storm or a clear sky at evening. Bring a camera or notebook, as this trip has moments you will want to keep for a long time.",
    "lost.23":"A lost item tends to turn up after you have let go of your worry. What you are waiting for, after a long drizzle, brings good news in a form that makes you smile, such as a thank-you message or the reply you had been waiting for.",
    "v.24":"A clear well that never runs dry because a spring feeds it is a picture of energy that can always be refilled. The surface stays clear when no one stirs the sediment. Readers take it that your source of strength, such as knowledge, calm and relationships, needs care so you have something to give.",
    "wish.24":"What you asked for succeeds when you first look after your own source of energy, such as resting enough, learning something new or spending time with people who refill you. This slip says what you asked for arrives more easily once you are ready to receive it.",
    "work.24":"Continuing to develop your skills, such as a short course, reading in your field or practicing a language, is digging the spring deeper. Seniors will see that you do not stand still and will hand you more challenging work as you are able.",
    "money.24":"Several income channels are like several springs. Explore your own skills that could be extended, such as taking side work in your strongest area or sharing knowledge as a small service. Start with a little, without affecting your main job.",
    "love.24":"Fill your own love cup first. Having a hobby you like and good friends means love does not have to carry the whole load. If you are single, you will draw balanced people more easily. If you are together, giving each other private space keeps the water clear.",
    "home.24":"At home, try looking after the ones who look after others, such as mothers, grandmothers or elders tired from household work, so they get some rest. Water stays clear when it is not stirred, and so does a household. A quiet corner for everyone matters.",
    "people.24":"Spend time with friends who refresh you and let you learn, and limit time with whatever drains you. With paperwork, prepare ahead so you do not have to rush and tire yourself. Take it one matter at a time.",
    "travel.24":"Travel to somewhere that refills your energy, such as the waterside, hills and forest, or a quiet library in another city. Do not over-pack the schedule. Leave time for your mind to soak things in, and you come back with strength for something new.",
    "lost.24":"A lost item can be found when your mind is still like water in a well. Take a deep breath and think through places one by one. What you are waiting for often comes from a spring you have tended, such as an old connection or a skill you have practiced.",
    "v.25":"The tortoise in Thai tales and belief is slow but steady, long-lived and never abandoning its goal. The picture of the tortoise reaching the finish before faster runners is a lesson that steadiness beats speed that keeps breaking off. Readers take it to be proud of your own pace.",
    "wish.25":{"t":"What you asked for will be reached by walking on without stopping, though not very soon. Walk a little each day and do not compare yourself with people who seem to be farther along. Your finish line will arrive in the way you have prepared for.",
    "c":true},
    "work.25":{"t":"Work steadily every day and do not rush to present a big result in a short time. Consistent quality builds a reputation by itself. If a coworker is promoted first, do not be discouraged, since each person's path runs at its own speed.",
    "c":true},
    "money.25":{"t":"Save a little but keep at it, and do not try to speed up your savings, since income built slowly is usually steadier. Cut one unneeded expense and put the difference into savings every month.",
    "c":true},
    "love.25":{"t":"Love forms gradually, so do not hurry to define the relationship. Let trust build up from small things every day. If you are single, do not worry if you have not met anyone. If you are together, give each other time and walk at a pace both are comfortable with.",
    "c":true},
    "home.25":"The household moves at a comfortable pace. Elders like steady routines. Cleaning or sorting things a little at a time together needs no long holiday, and children who learn step by step gain heart from not being rushed.",
    "people.25":"Friends of long standing are a treasure, so keep up the bond by checking in regularly. For paperwork, do it right the first time, step by step. There is no need to fear being slow, because correct steps do not have to come back for fixing.",
    "travel.25":{"t":"Set out early and without hurry. Allow enough time and drive or walk at an easy pace. It does not matter if you are slower than your friends. A trip not squeezed by the clock lets you see more of the details.",
    "c":true},
    "lost.25":{"t":"Search for a lost item slowly, one spot at a time, skipping none. Hurrying makes you overlook things. What you are waiting for may take longer than you think, so stay calm and follow up politely now and then.",
    "c":true},
    "v.26":"The golden gate opening to welcome a guest in Thai verse is a picture of a home ready for opportunity. The new guest means not only a person but news, work or a relationship just arrived. Readers take it that good fortune visits a home with its door open, since welcome belongs to those who prepare.",
    "wish.26":"What you asked for sits at the very favorable level. The gate is open, and the answer often comes as a person or an opportunity you had not imagined. Prepare your heart for something a little different from the picture you drew, since good things can arrive in an unfamiliar shape.",
    "work.26":"An interesting new job offer may come in. Study the details and compare them with what you truly want. Get your résumé and portfolio ready now, even if you are not planning to move, because knowing the market strengthens your bargaining position.",
    "money.26":{"t":"A new income channel opens, such as a new client, side work or a collaboration. Check how trustworthy it is and the payment terms before agreeing. Try starting with a small job to prove it before putting in a lot of time or money.",
    "c":true},
    "love.26":"There is a chance of meeting someone new and impressive, especially in a place you have never been or a group you never joined. Open the conversation with curiosity. If you are together, it suits taking your partner to meet new people together.",
    "home.26":"A guest may visit, or a new member may join the household, whether a relative, a friend or a pet. Get the home ready and prepare simple things to offer a guest. Elders will be pleased. If you are thinking of moving, interesting new options come in.",
    "people.26":{"t":"Many new people come in, so welcome them with friendliness but get to know them before trusting them with anything important. With money and documents, do not hand over personal details or sign for anyone at once. Check identity and terms fully first.",
    "c":true},
    "travel.26":"A trip to a new place or hosting a guest from afar brings an exciting experience. It suits trying a city you have never visited, food you have never eaten, or learning a new culture with an open mind and good manners.",
    "lost.26":"A lost item may come back through someone you never knew, such as a person who found it and gets in touch. Post politely in the community or at the place where it happened. What you are waiting for may arrive along with other opportunities that follow.",
    "v.27":"A potter turning clay on the wheel with one hand is a picture of skill born from practice. Formless clay slowly becomes a vessel that can be used. Readers take it that every piece made with intention carries the maker's hand, and anyone who sees it knows it has value.",
    "wish.27":"What you asked for will succeed through your own craft. This slip does not say wait for luck, but spend time making your work or skill finer. Careful work brings the thing you asked for.",
    "work.27":"Craft or creative work stands out. Try building a portfolio or a collection of pieces you are proud of. Seniors and clients will remember your handiwork. Stay open to feedback so you can polish it further.",
    "love.27":"Love built with intention is like shaping clay, needing two pairs of hands and time. Try doing something together, such as cooking, gardening or mending something. If you are single, you may meet someone who admires what you make.",
    "home.27":"The family's hands are all over the home. It suits doing things yourselves, such as painting, making small furniture or sewing. Elders appreciate what household members make, and the family ends up with meaningful things to use.",
    "people.27":"Friends with similar skills will swap techniques with you. With paperwork, neat handwriting or layout makes the recipient find it trustworthy, so check that documents are clean before sending.",
    "travel.27":"Travel to learn something new, such as a craft workshop, an art market or a local place of production, brings inspiration and new friends. Note down the techniques you see so you can use them later.",
    "lost.27":"A lost item may be a small thing used in your work, such as a tool, so search the toolbox, the work table and the corners where you like to set things. What you are waiting for is in process, so do your own part with care and the result will show.",
    "v.28":"The moon returning to full stands for one cycle completed. In Thai culture the full-moon day is when people make merit and review their lives. Fullness is both the end of one round and the start of the next. Readers take it to appreciate your success and give thanks before beginning something new.",
    "wish.28":"What you asked for sits at the very favorable level. Like the full moon when everything fits, the answer tends to come as a completion, with what you began ending beautifully. When that day comes, celebrate in a small way and thank those who walked with you.",
    "work.28":"A job closes in success. It suits handing over, writing up the lessons and thanking the team before starting the next project. A tidy handover lets your name be trusted in the new cycle as well.",
    "money.28":{"t":"Finances are balanced and settled. Review the yearly budget, clear small debts and set the next savings target. Take care that delight in the milestone does not carry you into spending over the budget on celebration, and keep part aside for the next round.",
    "c":true},
    "love.28":"Love is complete and warm. It suits celebrating an anniversary or looking back together at good memories. For those thinking of starting a family or an engagement, both families are ready to listen. If you are single, you can feel whole by yourself and open to someone new when ready.",
    "home.28":"The home is full and peaceful. It suits gathering relatives on an important day, telling old stories and making merit together. If you are thinking of moving, the anniversary of your stay may be a good moment to pass on or thank the old place before going to the new.",
    "people.28":"Relationships that have come around to a full cycle deserve thanks to those who helped all along. Paperwork that has dragged on tends to be completed. Check your copies and tidy the file once it is done.",
    "travel.28":"Coming back from a trip with happiness. A journey that marks an anniversary, such as returning to a place you went to together, or celebrating a success with a small trip, gives a full-hearted memory.",
    "lost.28":"A lost item has a chance of coming back whole, so count the full set again. What you are waiting for in rounds, such as exam results, a selection or closing an account, tends to complete at a moment when your heart is ready."};
  R.text.en.siamsee = T;
})(typeof globalThis !== "undefined" ? globalThis : this);
/* END depth en.siamsee */
